# Target path: <repo-root>/.husky/commit-msg
#
# Validates the commit message against commitlint.config.ts. "$1" is the path to the
# message file git passes to this hook — quote it; paths can contain spaces.
#
# `--no-install` is deliberate: without it, npx may go to the network mid-commit to fetch
# a missing binary, so a commit hangs (or fails offline) for a reason that looks nothing
# like a lint problem. If it errors with "command not found", the dev dependency is
# genuinely missing — run `npm install`, do not delete the flag.
npx --no-install commitlint --edit "$1"
